# The pinned upstreams, one per line: name url commit version
#
# Read by libs/fetch.sh and by tools/verify.sh. The commit is what the
# parent repository records as the submodule's gitlink, so `git submodule
# status` and this file must agree - verify.sh checks that they do, because
# a submodule silently advanced by a `git submodule update --remote` is a
# different measurement under the same name.
#
# Why each version is the one it is, which is NOT a detail:
#
#   mbedtls   3.6 IS THE LTS LINE AND IT IS PINNED DELIBERATELY. Mbed-TLS
#             4.x HAS NO library/aes.c AT ALL - AES moved to the separate
#             tf-psa-crypto repository - so a build "against the latest
#             Mbed-TLS" is not a build of this code. A shallow clone of the
#             default branch lands on 4.x and silently measures nothing,
#             which is exactly what happened while setting this up.
#
#   wolfssl   current stable. wolfssl/version.h ships in the repository, so
#             nothing has to be generated by autotools before building.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: ST's STM32 Cryptographic Library. There is no
# STMicroelectronics/x-cube-cryptolib repository, and STM32CubeL1 carries
# no crypto middleware - it ships inside X-CUBE-SBSFU. It can't be a
# submodule since there's no upstream to point one at, so it gets its own
# fetch path and a SHA-256 manifest instead. See libs/README.md.
mbedtls https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls.git 068ff080b369adfac81509f9b57b2afabaf82dc5 3.6.7
wolfssl https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl.git  3c5eead44904df64e6a5a1f4ebdce377d35a849a 5.9.4
